  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given 222 **binary** arrays AAA and BBB of length NNN. Binary arrays means that 0≤Ai,Bi≤10 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 10≤Ai​,Bi​≤1.\n\nIs it possible to convert AAA to BBB using the following operation as many times as you want:\n\n\nChoose index iii such that 1&lt;i&lt;N1 &lt; i &lt; N1&lt;i&lt;N and change AiA_iAi​ to Ai−1∣Ai+1A_{i - 1} | A_{i + 1}Ai−1​∣Ai+1​, where ∣|∣ represents the Bitwise OR Operator.\nPrint Yes or No accordingly.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the size of the arrays.\nThe second line contains NNN binary integers - A1,A2,…ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots A_NA1​,A2​,…AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN binary integers - B1,B2,…BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots B_NB1​,B2​,…BN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line Yes\\text{Yes}Yes or No\\text{No}No depending on if the answer is possible or not.\n\n\nIt is allowed to print each character on either case. For example, YES\\text{YES}YES, yes\\text{yes}yes, and yEs\\text{yEs}yEs will all be accepted.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "3≤N≤2⋅1053 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai,Bi≤10 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 10≤Ai​,Bi​≤1",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
